WEBVTT

00:02.430 --> 00:03.810
Good evening!

00:05.590 --> 00:06.930
A healer...

00:06.930 --> 00:08.730
What does he think he's doing here?

00:09.720 --> 00:12.740
<i>Maybe it's because of my robe, 
but I can feel them all staring.</i>

00:14.070 --> 00:16.160
Is the master available?

00:16.580 --> 00:17.670
<i>Here, too?</i>

00:17.670 --> 00:20.120
Hey, Luciel. What's going on?

00:20.820 --> 00:23.080
I'd like ten barrels of Substance X, please.

00:23.080 --> 00:26.040
Ten?! If you say so...

00:26.040 --> 00:29.750
<i>I think they're all staring 
for a different reason now.</i>

00:31.510 --> 00:35.450
By the way, since you're the maso-zombie
 healer, I have a favor to...

00:35.450 --> 00:37.690
er, a request to ask of you.

00:37.690 --> 00:39.140
What kind of request?

00:39.140 --> 00:42.890
I'd like you to take up your trade here
like you did in Merratoni.

00:44.810 --> 00:47.730
Unfortunately, I don't think I can

00:48.260 --> 00:51.800
since I'm currently working 
at church headquarters.

00:51.800 --> 00:56.110
Hmm, then what if I request 
treatment from you as an adventurer?

00:57.420 --> 01:00.830
<i>If there are adventurers in trouble,
I should lend a hand.</i>

01:00.830 --> 01:04.290
<i>That's what I promised in Merratoni.</i>

01:04.290 --> 01:08.040
<i>And maybe I can repay Master Brod
and the others this way.</i>

01:08.040 --> 01:10.810
I'm also an adventurer, after all,

01:10.810 --> 01:13.330
so if you call on me as such,
 I can accommodate.

01:13.330 --> 01:16.890
Really?! All right, first, your Substance X!

01:16.890 --> 01:18.350
Wait right there.

01:19.260 --> 01:21.300
What's going on?

01:21.300 --> 01:24.750
Recently, some very high-level 
monsters have been appearing.

01:24.750 --> 01:26.640
Lots of folks have suffered grave injuries.

01:26.640 --> 01:29.480
Is that why the master is looking so down?

01:29.480 --> 01:32.660
The adventurers are like family to him.

01:32.660 --> 01:34.900
Why don't they go to a clinic?

01:35.530 --> 01:38.490
You expect them to cough up gold
when they're terribly injured?!

01:38.490 --> 01:40.570
Do you <i>want</i> them to 
become slaves or something?

01:41.600 --> 01:43.490
Milty. That's enough.

01:43.980 --> 01:47.160
It's hard to explain. 
Will you fulfill my request?

01:48.420 --> 01:50.130
I don't come cheap.

01:50.920 --> 01:53.340
It'll cost one silver coin per person.

01:53.660 --> 01:57.260
I won't charge any more than that. 
My price is firm!

02:04.470 --> 02:08.770
<b>The Great Cleric</b>

02:05.600 --> 02:08.770
A Salaryman's <b>Path </b>to <b>Surviving Another World</b>

03:32.980 --> 03:36.230
#10 The Secret of Substance X

03:36.230 --> 03:38.960
Hey, hang in there!

03:38.960 --> 03:41.960
It's too late... I'm done for...

03:42.710 --> 03:45.320
We're out of options.
I'm taking you to a clinic.

03:45.320 --> 03:49.790
Idiot... I ain't made of money.

03:50.420 --> 03:53.950
I really had a blast with you guys...

03:53.950 --> 03:54.960
Hey!

03:56.760 --> 03:59.600
I don't care who...
Please, somebody help!

04:00.490 --> 04:02.530
There's quite a few of them.

04:02.530 --> 04:03.510
Can you handle it?

04:03.510 --> 04:06.010
Yes. Let me take a look first.

04:06.010 --> 04:08.720
Hey! What the hell're you doing here?!

04:08.720 --> 04:11.010
It's one of those cold, heartless healers!

04:11.010 --> 04:12.310
Go to hell!

04:12.310 --> 04:13.940
Get out of here!

04:13.940 --> 04:15.020
No, kill him!

04:15.020 --> 04:16.770
<i>Eek!</i>

04:16.770 --> 04:19.530
Quiet down, you fools!

04:20.950 --> 04:24.150
This guy... I mean,
this distinguished individual

04:24.150 --> 04:26.490
is the very urban legend from Merratoni!

04:26.490 --> 04:29.320
The maso-zombie healer!

04:31.100 --> 04:33.910
He says he'll help for a single silver coin.

04:33.910 --> 04:36.730
If you got a problem with that, 
<i>you</i> get out of here!

04:36.730 --> 04:39.010
Is he truly the legendary 
maso-zombie healer?

04:39.010 --> 04:41.260
So those weren't just tall tales?

04:41.710 --> 04:44.590
Will you really help us for one silver coin?

04:44.590 --> 04:48.940
If he's seriously the legendary maso-zombie,
 we might all be saved!

04:48.940 --> 04:51.220
Maso-zombie-sama...

04:51.780 --> 04:54.440
Maso-zombie-sama! Hurry and treat us!

04:54.440 --> 04:55.130
Wait a—

04:55.130 --> 04:58.110
The masochist! The masochist!

04:56.690 --> 04:57.550
Eh?

04:58.110 --> 04:59.320
What?

04:58.360 --> 05:01.620
Zombie! Zombie!

05:01.620 --> 05:04.700
The masochist! The masochist!

05:02.230 --> 05:04.700
<i>I don't like this one bit!</i>

05:04.700 --> 05:08.750
<i>At this rate, I'll be stuck with 
the zombie nickname forever!</i>

05:09.660 --> 05:11.330
Please listen!

05:11.330 --> 05:14.990
I do not wish to take work away from clinics,

05:14.990 --> 05:18.130
so I will not be able to treat you every time,

05:18.130 --> 05:22.800
but please don't riot or attack the clinics
 for being too expensive.

05:22.800 --> 05:27.590
I can only help out because I happened
 to be here picking up Substance X.

05:27.590 --> 05:31.560
Now, I'll treat you all with three conditions.

05:31.560 --> 05:33.790
It's one silver coin per person.

05:33.790 --> 05:38.290
And if someone with the church, 
like the pope, the Valkyries,

05:38.290 --> 05:41.270
or I get into trouble, I ask that 
you do what you can to help.

05:41.270 --> 05:44.930
Lastly, nicknames involving "zombie" 
and "masochist" are now off-limits!

05:44.930 --> 05:47.990
I need you to call me something
I can actually go by!

05:47.990 --> 05:49.070
Are we clear?

05:49.070 --> 05:51.080
Yeah!

05:51.080 --> 05:53.940
In that case, I'll begin the treatment.

05:55.250 --> 05:57.380
O holy touch of healing.

05:57.380 --> 05:59.230
O breath of the mother of this great land.

05:59.720 --> 06:02.660
O Lord, I offer up my magic...

06:02.660 --> 06:05.120
Bring relief as from the breath of an angel.

06:05.660 --> 06:07.330
Area high heal!

06:11.220 --> 06:13.390
It's gone! The pain's gone!

06:13.390 --> 06:15.370
All right! I'm healed!

06:15.370 --> 06:16.910
Thank you, Masochist-sama!

06:16.910 --> 06:19.460
Idiot! "Masochist" is off-limits!

06:21.060 --> 06:22.770
So let's give him another nickname.

06:22.770 --> 06:26.370
He treated us for cheap, 
so how about "The Cheap Healer"?

06:22.980 --> 06:23.480
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:23.480 --> 06:23.980
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:23.980 --> 06:24.480
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:24.480 --> 06:24.980
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:24.980 --> 06:25.480
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:25.480 --> 06:25.980
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:25.980 --> 06:26.440
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:25.980 --> 06:30.950
<b>The Cheap Healer</b>

06:26.370 --> 06:28.790
The Healers' Guild would 
definitely veto that.

06:26.440 --> 06:26.940
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:26.940 --> 06:27.440
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:27.440 --> 06:27.950
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:27.950 --> 06:28.450
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:28.450 --> 06:28.950
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:28.790 --> 06:31.090
Well, they say he likes to fight,

06:28.950 --> 06:29.450
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:29.450 --> 06:29.950
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:29.950 --> 06:30.450
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:30.450 --> 06:30.950
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:30.950 --> 06:31.450
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:30.990 --> 06:32.950
<b>The Battle-Crazed Healer</b>

06:31.090 --> 06:32.950
so how about "The Battle-Crazed Healer"?

06:31.450 --> 06:31.950
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:31.950 --> 06:32.450
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:32.450 --> 06:32.950
<b>BA-DUMP</b>

06:32.950 --> 06:34.920
Neither one has the right ring to it.

06:34.920 --> 06:37.330
"Maso-zombie" just fits too perfectly.

06:37.330 --> 06:40.080
<i>They're having a whole meeting 
about my nickname...</i>

06:40.080 --> 06:42.620
He's real distinguished,
so maybe "The Saint"?

06:41.170 --> 06:46.260
<b>The Saint</b>

06:42.620 --> 06:44.820
He's young, though. That's so stuffy.

06:44.820 --> 06:46.110
<i>It's definitely stuffy.</i>

06:46.110 --> 06:47.590
How about "Weirdo Healer"?

06:46.300 --> 06:49.260
<b>Weirdo Healer</b>

06:47.590 --> 06:49.260
<i>That's no better than "masochist"!</i>

06:49.260 --> 06:53.550
I've got it! He's weird,
but he's also like a saint.

06:53.600 --> 06:55.490
<b>Weird Saint</b>

06:55.490 --> 06:56.740
So "St. Weirdo"!

06:55.680 --> 06:58.020
<b>St. Weirdo</b>

06:56.740 --> 06:58.020
<i>Excuse me?!</i>

06:58.020 --> 06:59.680
That's the one!

06:59.680 --> 07:02.890
St. Weirdo! St. Weirdo! Let's hear it for...

07:02.480 --> 07:06.730
<b>St. Weirdo! St. Weirdo!</b>

07:02.890 --> 07:05.830
St. Weirdo! St. Weirdo!

07:05.830 --> 07:08.450
<i>Hey! What kind of cheer is that?!</i>

07:08.450 --> 07:11.200
<i>Adventurers are so bad at giving nicknames!</i>

07:11.200 --> 07:14.780
"Maso-zombie" still has
the best ring to it, though.

07:14.780 --> 07:15.990
Tell me about it.

07:15.990 --> 07:17.560
<i>Gong!</i>

07:16.080 --> 07:18.540
<b>Gong...</b>

07:21.800 --> 07:23.080
Good morning.

07:23.080 --> 07:25.210
Oh, good morning.

07:25.600 --> 07:27.240
You're later than usual.

07:27.240 --> 07:32.010
Yeah, I went to see the Valkyries off
 since they've been helping me out.

07:34.550 --> 07:36.100
What's all this fanfare?

07:36.100 --> 07:39.380
Crowds don't usually 
come out for us like this.

07:39.380 --> 07:42.310
Go for it! Just like Masochist-sama!

07:42.310 --> 07:43.270
Like St. Weirdo!

07:43.270 --> 07:44.380
Like Zombie-sama!

07:44.380 --> 07:45.770
Just like St. Weirdo!

07:53.480 --> 07:55.570
So you're heading to the labyrinth now?

07:56.000 --> 07:58.710
Will you be returning around the usual time?

07:58.710 --> 08:01.290
Actually, I'm thinking about 
staying there for a while.

08:02.390 --> 08:04.670
I can't allow you do to 
something that dangerous!

08:04.670 --> 08:10.510
But I really only come back to sleep. 
I have plenty of food in my magic sack.

08:10.510 --> 08:12.090
That isn't the issue!

08:12.470 --> 08:15.830
It'll be fine. If I defeat 
the monsters in the main chamber,

08:15.830 --> 08:19.740
there aren't any more until I open the door.

08:20.890 --> 08:24.940
In that case, just be sure 
to return here once a week.

08:24.940 --> 08:28.780
And don't overdo it.
I don't want to see you dead.

08:29.650 --> 08:30.970
You got it!

08:30.970 --> 08:33.110
My mottos are "make it out alive"

08:33.510 --> 08:35.070
and "don't die!"

08:38.620 --> 08:40.380
Then take care. See you soon.

08:40.380 --> 08:42.500
Yeah. I'm off now!

08:44.570 --> 08:47.840
<i>Don't you die on me, Luciel-kun.</i>

08:49.530 --> 08:51.130
Heya, I'm back!

08:51.130 --> 08:54.140
Already?! It hasn't even been a week yet!

08:54.140 --> 08:55.050
Huh?

08:55.050 --> 08:58.110
Well, I'm glad to see you're safe.

08:58.110 --> 09:00.260
My internal clock must be off.

09:00.260 --> 09:04.340
Oh, that's right. I have 
your new weapons and armor,

09:04.340 --> 09:06.610
as well as some magical items from the pope.

09:06.610 --> 09:08.000
For real?

09:15.110 --> 09:19.990
<b>Paladin's Armor</b>

09:15.620 --> 09:18.130
Ooh, this is so cool!

09:18.130 --> 09:19.460
There's also this.

09:19.990 --> 09:22.450
<b>Angel's Pillow</b>

09:21.470 --> 09:22.450
A pillow?

09:22.450 --> 09:24.370
It's an angel's pillow.

09:24.370 --> 09:27.650
It helps you sleep soundly so 
you're fully refreshed the next day.

09:27.650 --> 09:29.210
Wow!

09:29.210 --> 09:31.970
So, what will you do for the rest of the day?

09:31.970 --> 09:34.910
I'm going to go buy some food 
and then head back in.

09:34.910 --> 09:37.380
I know I keep saying this, 
but don't overdo it.

09:37.890 --> 09:40.350
And be sure to come back within one week.

09:40.350 --> 09:42.030
Understood!

09:44.630 --> 09:46.440
I thought you'd be back.

09:47.650 --> 09:50.320
Isn't today St. Weirdo's free day?

09:50.320 --> 09:52.030
St. Weirdo's free day?

09:52.030 --> 09:55.420
Yeah. I reckoned you'd be out of Substance X,

09:55.420 --> 09:57.820
and you mentioned you get one day off a week.

09:57.820 --> 09:59.960
I'm surprised you remembered.

09:59.960 --> 10:03.790
If I couldn't remember that much, I wouldn't 
be worth my weight as guild master.

10:03.790 --> 10:06.750
So why are you always in the kitchen?

10:07.150 --> 10:08.220
I enjoy it!

10:08.220 --> 10:10.040
I see...

10:10.040 --> 10:13.110
Oh, right. May I ask you 
to send another letter?

10:13.110 --> 10:14.960
Yeah, sure, sure.

10:15.320 --> 10:17.590
<i>I haven't gotten any responses yet, though.</i>

10:17.590 --> 10:19.620
Oh, it's St. Weirdo.

10:20.610 --> 10:23.410
Today after healing, you're 
joining a mock battle, right?

10:23.410 --> 10:26.810
Nice! I can show St. Weirdo how 
much the training has helped me.

10:27.120 --> 10:30.630
Whatever we call him, there's no 
way I'm gonna lose to a healer.

10:30.630 --> 10:31.810
Yeah!

10:31.810 --> 10:34.840
<i>I guess that St. Weirdo thing 
is gonna stick...</i>

10:34.840 --> 10:38.160
They're all worked up 
since they get to fight you.

10:38.160 --> 10:39.280
Is that right?

10:39.710 --> 10:42.280
Since they've been training 
and practicing more,

10:42.280 --> 10:45.240
the number of deaths and failed 
missions has dropped sharply.

10:45.240 --> 10:46.950
I'm very glad to hear that.

10:47.300 --> 10:50.160
To prepare for this day, they've 
all been taking high-ranking jobs

10:50.160 --> 10:53.920
and fighting strong monsters. 
It's been nothing but good news.

10:53.920 --> 10:56.420
Look, it's St. Weirdo.

10:56.420 --> 10:58.250
Oh, Elitz-dono.

10:58.250 --> 11:00.670
You getting buddy-buddy with A-ranks?

11:00.670 --> 11:03.870
Yeah, ever since this 
guy treated my injuries.

11:03.870 --> 11:06.890
Well, you've also taught me 
a lot since then.

11:07.250 --> 11:10.440
How about that physical
enhancement skill I showed you?

11:10.440 --> 11:12.480
That's still difficult for me.

11:12.910 --> 11:17.670
I have to focus my magic
and quickly circulate it through my body...

11:17.670 --> 11:19.440
Physical enhancement!

11:21.080 --> 11:24.170
But it isn't as easy as it sounds.

11:25.640 --> 11:28.750
Yeah, even though your 
magic control skill is so high.

11:28.750 --> 11:32.610
Also, are you still stuck at level 1?

11:32.610 --> 11:34.010
That doesn't seem right.

11:34.010 --> 11:36.630
It's because I haven't defeated any monsters.

11:36.630 --> 11:40.470
<i>I mean, I have, but they were all illusions.</i>

11:40.470 --> 11:42.830
Man, what a waste!

11:42.830 --> 11:46.720
If you can fight that well, 
you'd be a real diamond in the rough!

11:47.470 --> 11:48.930
St. Weirdo!

11:48.930 --> 11:50.810
Everyone's ready for their treatment.

11:50.810 --> 11:52.950
Okay! I'm on my way.

11:56.180 --> 11:57.850
Purification!

11:57.850 --> 11:58.920
Recover!

11:59.390 --> 12:00.690
Dispel!

12:00.690 --> 12:02.490
Area high heal!

12:05.150 --> 12:07.390
Okay, all done!

12:07.390 --> 12:09.680
Everyone feels better now, right?

12:09.680 --> 12:12.870
Yes! Thank you very much!

12:12.870 --> 12:14.800
Okay, if any of you have news of Merratoni

12:14.800 --> 12:18.480
or word about the Valkyrie paladin 
regiment, raise your hand.

12:18.480 --> 12:19.340
I do!

12:19.340 --> 12:22.540
I've heard that the Valkyries are all safe.

12:22.540 --> 12:24.550
Phew. That's good.

12:24.950 --> 12:27.550
But I heard that there were 
deaths among the templars.

12:28.560 --> 12:32.170
Over here! I know something about Merratoni.

12:32.170 --> 12:32.850
Go ahead.

12:33.300 --> 12:35.540
I've heard that the Whirlwind 
is out of control.

12:35.540 --> 12:36.700
The Whirlwind?!

12:36.700 --> 12:40.110
He keeps kidnapping adventurers and 
dragging them to his training hall.

12:41.230 --> 12:43.530
Master Brod!

12:43.530 --> 12:46.920
Hey, I heard that he used to 
be focused on one disciple,

12:46.920 --> 12:48.850
so things were okay then.

12:48.850 --> 12:52.980
But then that disciple left and now 
other adventurers are taking the heat.

12:52.980 --> 12:54.850
<i>Sorry, guys...</i>

12:54.850 --> 12:56.530
Then there's that bear chef!

12:56.530 --> 12:57.380
<i>Bear chef?</i>

12:57.380 --> 12:59.540
He isn't just making 
people drink Substance X.

12:59.540 --> 13:02.960
He's been inventing new recipes 
with it to make people eat!

13:03.920 --> 13:06.760
<i>Gulgar-san, what are you thinking?</i>

13:06.760 --> 13:11.560
Oh, and another thing. A receptionist at 
the Adventurers' Guild is getting married.

13:12.810 --> 13:14.260
Actually, multiple receptionists are.

13:14.260 --> 13:16.190
What was that? Tell me more.

13:16.190 --> 13:19.650
Well, it sounds like the guys 
who captured the receptionists' hearts

13:19.650 --> 13:22.360
are A-rank beastfolk 
adventurers or something.

13:22.360 --> 13:25.170
But who? Which receptionists?!

13:25.170 --> 13:27.070
Um, I don't actually know.

13:27.070 --> 13:28.530
Who is it?!

13:28.530 --> 13:30.650
<i>"Multiple" means at least two of them!</i>

13:30.650 --> 13:32.490
<i>So who and who else?!</i>

13:32.490 --> 13:36.280
<i>If they're marrying beastfolk,
could one of them be Nanaella-san?</i>

13:36.870 --> 13:41.350
<i>Now that I think of it, is this why 
they haven't responded to my letters?</i>

13:41.350 --> 13:42.880
<i>Huh?!</i>

13:44.520 --> 13:45.710
<i>At least...</i>

13:46.060 --> 13:49.560
<i>At the very least, 
please invite me to the wedding.</i>

13:51.800 --> 13:54.720
<i>It's been half a year since 
I beat the level twenty boss.</i>

13:55.560 --> 13:57.340
Area high heal!

14:01.490 --> 14:05.670
Phew. Looks like a total victory this time.

14:05.670 --> 14:10.790
<i>Thanks to all my training, I finally 
vanquished the boss on the thirtieth level.</i>

14:13.100 --> 14:14.830
I'm so glad you're all right.

14:15.250 --> 14:17.160
Thank you for coming back to me alive.

14:17.160 --> 14:19.790
Please... This is embarrassing.

14:21.390 --> 14:23.560
You really did an amazing job this time.

14:23.560 --> 14:27.120
You earned 426,549 points.

14:27.120 --> 14:30.840
So that robe I bought the other day 
after five trips to the labyrinth...

14:30.840 --> 14:33.100
I could afford another one of those?

14:33.100 --> 14:34.420
You sure could.

14:34.420 --> 14:38.810
And if you have points left over, you might 
think about stocking up on magic potions.

14:38.810 --> 14:40.120
Good idea.

14:40.120 --> 14:44.730
Your magic sack can fit as many as you want,
 so it wouldn't hurt to have them.

14:44.730 --> 14:48.280
I depend on magic for most fights, 
so that could be a real lifesaver.

14:48.280 --> 14:52.390
Just this run, I would've been
in trouble without area high heal.

14:52.390 --> 14:55.740
What? You're so young
and you can use area high heal?

14:55.740 --> 14:58.690
Luciel-kun, have you 
been lying about your age?

14:58.690 --> 15:01.850
The first time I visited 
the Healers' Guild at age fifteen,

15:01.850 --> 15:03.960
I didn't even know how to use heal.

15:04.320 --> 15:08.170
Then have you gotten your hands 
on some kind of strange drug?

15:08.170 --> 15:10.380
Huh? No, that's not even...

15:10.380 --> 15:11.760
Oh!

15:10.510 --> 15:11.760
Substance X

15:11.760 --> 15:17.080
Well then, when you make your report to 
the pope, you can come clean and repent.

15:17.080 --> 15:17.720
Okay.

15:17.720 --> 15:23.690
<b>D
R
A
A
A
A
A
G</b>

15:18.120 --> 15:23.690
Maybe I can at least learn something about 
all this Substance X I've been drinking...

15:24.500 --> 15:29.690
You mean to say you've already
reached the thirtieth level on your own?

15:30.210 --> 15:33.570
I must say, I never expected this.

15:33.570 --> 15:35.410
I applaud your efforts.

15:35.900 --> 15:38.330
It seems your magic powers have also grown

15:38.330 --> 15:41.020
much more powerful since we first met.

15:41.720 --> 15:43.880
I have a report to make regarding that.

15:44.290 --> 15:49.340
He's apparently been drinking a beverage 
called Substance X for two and a half years.

15:49.710 --> 15:50.930
This is it.

15:51.680 --> 15:52.910
Gross!

15:53.260 --> 15:54.490
Put that away immediately!

15:54.490 --> 15:55.590
A-All right!

15:55.590 --> 15:56.920
Is it poison?

15:56.920 --> 15:58.060
N-No.

15:58.060 --> 16:01.000
<i>Maybe I should cast purification anyway...</i>

16:01.520 --> 16:06.320
It's not poison. It's something 
they serve at the Adventurers' Guild.

16:06.320 --> 16:11.190
They say it's produced when you cast magic
 on a special item crafted by a sage.

16:11.190 --> 16:13.340
At the Adventurers' Guild?

16:13.340 --> 16:16.490
Wait. What is the name of this drink?

16:16.490 --> 16:19.170
I know it as Substance X.

16:19.170 --> 16:22.720
It's something they force
new adventurer's to consume.

16:22.720 --> 16:28.420
Hmm. I believe it was originally created
to awaken people's latent talents.

16:28.420 --> 16:33.710
It's made from medicinal herbs, 
dragon's heart, and spirit water,

16:33.710 --> 16:35.300
and crafted into a pill.

16:35.300 --> 16:38.480
<i>A pill? That'd be much easier to take.</i>

16:38.480 --> 16:40.800
A sage claimed to have developed

16:40.800 --> 16:44.860
a magical device to replicate
 the recipe at any time.

16:45.600 --> 16:50.620
But what came out instead was a liquid,
so he renamed it.

16:50.620 --> 16:51.610
Why?

16:51.610 --> 16:57.450
I believe it was called Substance X 
when it was in pill form,

16:57.450 --> 17:00.790
but the liquid version of it 
was so unpalatable

17:00.790 --> 17:04.000
that its creator changed its name to...

17:04.160 --> 17:06.920
<b>God's Lament</b>

17:04.990 --> 17:06.920
God's Lament.

17:06.920 --> 17:08.600
It certainly tastes horrible.

17:08.600 --> 17:11.990
I would believe even God
would lament its flavor.

17:11.990 --> 17:13.870
I drink three mugs a day after my meals,

17:13.870 --> 17:17.080
and I've been doing so for two and half years.

17:17.080 --> 17:18.010
Huh?

17:18.010 --> 17:20.160
Is that the truth?

17:20.160 --> 17:23.480
Yes. Life in this world is so fragile,

17:23.480 --> 17:26.460
so I felt I should do
whatever I could to survive.

17:26.460 --> 17:27.440
Hmm.

17:27.920 --> 17:32.400
There are no side effects and just drinking
it makes you strong, so how could I not?

17:32.400 --> 17:34.170
I see now.

17:34.170 --> 17:39.120
Your efforts and that hardship
are what have allowed you to grow so.

17:39.120 --> 17:41.450
I can't believe you can drink that sludge.

17:41.730 --> 17:43.980
Pretty impressive, Luciel-kun.

17:43.980 --> 17:45.330
Cattleya-san?

17:45.330 --> 17:50.420
So, Luciel, will you tell me what kinds 
of monsters you encountered this time?

17:50.420 --> 17:54.500
Yes. There were three wights 
and five ghost knights.

17:54.500 --> 17:57.530
I evaded them, eventually 
defeating them with area high heal.

17:57.530 --> 17:59.890
You're able to use that at your age?

18:00.540 --> 18:04.430
You may yet become a sage yourself one day.

18:04.430 --> 18:05.820
I will do my best.

18:05.820 --> 18:09.600
Now then, bring me the items 
the monsters dropped.

18:13.220 --> 18:16.280
Oh, these are from... those three girls.

18:16.280 --> 18:18.100
<i>What three girls?</i>

18:18.540 --> 18:20.070
That is all for today.

18:20.070 --> 18:23.360
I will deliver your reward 
to Cattleya in good time.

18:23.740 --> 18:27.610
Do continue to explore the labyrinth.

18:35.460 --> 18:37.070
Good morning!

18:37.070 --> 18:39.990
Luciel-kun? Morning.

18:41.210 --> 18:43.260
The pope sent this letter.

18:44.590 --> 18:45.820
What is it?

18:45.820 --> 18:50.710
It details the effects of God's Lament, 
also known as Substance X.

18:50.710 --> 18:54.320
Wow. I'll read it later in the labyrinth.

18:54.650 --> 18:55.790
I'm off.

18:56.650 --> 18:58.710
Um, Luciel-kun?

18:58.710 --> 18:59.570
Yes?

18:59.570 --> 19:01.490
Good luck.

19:01.490 --> 19:04.780
If you're ever having a hard time,
I'll be here for you.

19:04.780 --> 19:08.610
Sure. Thanks a lot.

19:10.230 --> 19:12.140
Now then, what's it say?

19:12.140 --> 19:19.010
"This is a direct reproduction of the notes 
on God's Lament, also known as Substance X.

19:20.570 --> 19:22.260
Humans have three major primal urges.

19:22.770 --> 19:26.510
They desire sleep, they desire food,
 and they desire sex.

19:26.510 --> 19:30.770
But those desires tend to wane
in those who devote themselves to the Church.

19:31.310 --> 19:34.230
I thought this medicine could be as a beacon to such devotees

19:34.230 --> 19:37.730
to prevent them from losing
 the joys of living.

19:38.290 --> 19:41.450
It has the effect of amplifying 
the three primal urges.

19:42.030 --> 19:44.820
It also produced some unexpected side effects.

19:45.450 --> 19:50.830
It seems to protect the body from various 
maladies, revitalize cells while sleeping,

19:50.830 --> 19:54.480
and facilitate skill growth as well."

19:54.990 --> 19:58.780
Wow, Substance X is this amazing?

19:58.780 --> 20:01.550
"However, a tragedy occurred.

20:02.990 --> 20:05.660
There was a wave of criticism 
due to its unbearably bad smell.

20:05.660 --> 20:09.850
It was deemed unfit for the Church 
and slated for disposal.

20:07.350 --> 20:09.850
Out!

20:08.390 --> 20:09.850
<b><i>Gong!</i></b>

20:09.850 --> 20:14.250
Yet this medicine was the reason 
I was allowed to become a sage.

20:14.250 --> 20:18.220
So I asked the Adventurers' Guild 
headquarters if I could leave it with them.

20:18.940 --> 20:22.740
If any beginners are curious about the effects, 
I'd like it to be available for them to drink.

20:22.740 --> 20:29.780
I pray that this God's Lament may one day 
become the item that saves the world."

20:30.500 --> 20:34.260
Huh. What's on this other page?

20:34.970 --> 20:38.460
The results of a study 
on Substance X's effects, huh?

20:38.460 --> 20:39.800
<b>Desire to Sleep</b>

20:38.460 --> 20:39.800
<b>Desire for Sex</b>

20:38.460 --> 20:40.800
<b>Desire to Eat</b>

20:39.720 --> 20:45.330
The actual effect of Substance X
is increasing one of the three primal urges

20:40.460 --> 20:41.880
<b>Desire to Sleep</b>

20:41.550 --> 20:42.800
<b>Desire for Sex</b>

20:45.330 --> 20:51.950
and transforming that energy to enhance
 one's overall physical ability.

20:52.510 --> 20:57.610
That's a pretty big secret. 
So it sacrifices a primal urge, eh?

20:57.610 --> 20:59.110
Come to think of it...

20:59.110 --> 21:02.030
Desire to eat

20:59.670 --> 21:02.310
I've got an appetite.

21:02.110 --> 21:04.990
Desire to sleep

21:02.310 --> 21:05.070
I love to sleep.

21:05.070 --> 21:10.160
Desire for sex

21:06.290 --> 21:09.750
And sexual desire... Wait, sexual desire?

21:11.790 --> 21:12.790
<b>Sexual</b>

21:11.790 --> 21:14.420
Sexual desire...

21:12.790 --> 21:16.290
<b>Sexual Desire</b>

21:14.420 --> 21:16.600
Now that I think about it, I've got none.

21:22.430 --> 21:25.050
Absolutely none! Not any at all!

21:25.500 --> 21:28.370
Wait, was that because she felt sorry for me?!

21:28.370 --> 21:32.330
Does she basically think 
I'm impotent or something?!

21:32.330 --> 21:34.600
Like I'm already in celibate sage mode?!

21:33.390 --> 21:34.600
<i>I'm in sage mode?!</i>

21:34.600 --> 21:37.730
I mean, this world is full of babes.

21:37.730 --> 21:40.690
But I've never once felt 
turned on around them!

21:41.360 --> 21:43.960
S-Still, even if I haven't been turned on,

21:43.960 --> 21:46.110
they've definitely caught my eye before.

21:46.110 --> 21:49.390
Absolutely. Definitely. So I'm okay.

21:49.390 --> 21:51.990
I'm... totally okay.

21:52.600 --> 21:54.450
Okay.

21:54.450 --> 21:57.920
Once I make it through the labyrinth, 
I'm going to fall in love!

21:57.920 --> 22:00.160
Oh yeah!

22:00.560 --> 22:04.640
Except I still haven't gotten responses 
to any of my letters...

22:09.590 --> 22:12.010
Training! Training!

22:12.010 --> 22:14.890
It's training time!

22:14.890 --> 22:19.120
All for my future!

23:55.860 --> 23:58.080
Oh, dear Luciel.

23:58.080 --> 24:02.370
You drank all that Substance X 
and now have zero sex drive?

24:02.370 --> 24:05.210
Next time: "Trouble in St. Shurule."

24:04.670 --> 24:09.880
#11 Trouble in St. Shurule

24:05.520 --> 24:09.160
At this rate, you might 
change jobs and become a sage.
